From: Clint Goudie-Nice <clint-goudie-nice@example.net>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 04:06:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] seastone: sai.profile guards for the Tomahawk-1 HFTel
 and stats-ext calls

202511's orchagent asks the SAI for streaming-telemetry capability at
start (HFTelOrch::isSupportedHFTel -> sai_query_stats_st_capability),
which 202505's did not. On a BCM56960 (Tomahawk-1) the Broadcom SAI
answers by dereferencing an uninitialised streaming-telemetry driver
in brcm_sai_st_pd_ctr_cap_list_get: syncd dies with SIGSEGV and swss
crash-loops (sonic-sairedis#1788, sonic-buildimage#28127). The same
function is in every libsaibcm 202511 can install on this box
(13.2.1.36, 13.2.1.100 legacy-TH, 14.3.0.0.0.0.41.1 XGS).

202511's sairedis carries the runtime opt-out (#1795, backport of
#1788/#1789): SAI_STATS_ST_CAPABILITY_SUPPORTED=0 nulls the query, and
SAI_STATS_EXT_SWITCH_SUPPORTED=0 the switch get_stats_ext that crashes
the same way during flex-counter polling. The Arista 7060CX-32S (the
other Tomahawk-1 in the tree) has carried both since #26201/#26217;
the Seastone profiles never got them. This is the DX010 part of
sonic-net/sonic-buildimage#28160 (open, against master), applied to
all eight Seastone HwSKUs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
